cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HALO: companion datasets and code for Modern Biostatistics for the Health Sciences and Biostatistics with R & AI"
message: "If you use these datasets or this code, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Gharibvand
    given-names: Lida
    name-suffix: "MS, PhD"
    affiliation: "School of Allied Health Professions, Loma Linda University Health"
abstract: >-
  HALO (Heart And Lipid Outcomes) is an original simulated health system created
  for teaching biostatistics and health research methods. It comprises a
  randomized lipid-lowering trial of 2,000 participants, a clinic panel of 6,000
  patients, a long-format repeated-measures file, a hospital encounter extract, a
  patient experience survey, a ward log and five years of service-area vital
  statistics. The files carry documented planted errors so that data quality can
  be taught by finding faults rather than by describing them. Nothing in HALO is
  real: no participant, clinic, ward, physician or treatment in it exists, and no
  figure computed from it describes any real population.
keywords:
  - biostatistics
  - health research methods
  - simulated data
  - teaching datasets
  - research design
  - R
